WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.533
Book 13 sorts every change into lanes,

2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:05.738
and each lane lands
somewhere on these products.

3
00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:09.912
Most of this mapping is our
inference, so read it as a proposal.

4
00:00:09.912 --> 00:00:14.787
The autonomous lane maps to SailPoint
lifecycle states and birthright access,

5
00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:18.037
and to ServiceNow's
pre-authorized standard changes.

6
00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:21.980
The gated lane is a SailPoint
access request with an approver,

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.913
or a ServiceNow normal change.

8
00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:27.367
Human decisions are certifications
and the change board,

9
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:32.188
and one highpoint there is documented:
unsigned revoke decisions aren't applied.

10
00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:36.613
Certificates sit with neither product;
they stay with the certificate platform.

11
00:00:36.613 --> 00:00:40.505
And a disconnected application
becomes a declared exception,

12
00:00:40.505 --> 00:00:43.424
with a ticket, a recorded
session and an end date.

13
00:00:43.424 --> 00:00:44.620
Now the gaps.
